The decision is particularly appropriate for TrueCost because your own repository audit shows that this is not one simple shopping interface: the target architecture spans 32 providers across Grocery, Food, Pharmacy, Shopping, Mobility, Travel, Finance and Productivity/SaaS, while implementation maturity currently differs materially by category. Grocery has the deepest end-to-end stack and real replay evidence; Shopping has a stronger backend stack but no equivalent real capture corpus; most other categories currently have connectors/scrapers without the same MCP/workflow maturity. The UI therefore needs one powerful common design language **without pretending every domain has identical backend capability today**. fileciteturn0file4

